  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"10.5.2\"\n\npackage:\n  name: graphblas\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/DrTimothyAldenDavis/GraphBLAS/archive/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 1307dd9ace59f4efb1544f74c745e31886362354286226d709749dab02b0f69e\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    # No C++ compiler: with Fortran and CUDA off, GraphBLAS never enables C++,\n    # and requiring one only added a libstdcxx/libcxx run dependency.\n    - ${{ compiler(\"c\") }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - cmake\n    # Not Ninja on unix: it breaks the cross-built JIT package (see build.sh)\n    - if: unix\n      then: make\n      else: ninja\n  # MSVC builds use its own OpenMP runtime (vcomp140.dll, from vc14_runtime),\n  # so llvm-openmp is never linked on Windows.\n  host:\n    - if: not win\n      then: llvm-openmp\n  run:\n    - if: not win\n      then: llvm-openmp\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage(\"graphblas\", upper_bound=\"x.x\") }}\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      include:\n        - suitesparse/GraphBLAS.h\n      lib:\n        - graphblas\n      files:\n        exists:\n          - if: unix\n            then: lib/cmake/GraphBLAS/GraphBLASConfig.cmake\n            else: Library/lib/cmake/GraphBLAS/GraphBLASConfig.cmake\n        not_exists:\n          - if: unix\n            then: lib/libgraphblas.a\n            else: Library/lib/graphblas_static.lib\n          # Built and run during the build to generate the JIT package\n          - if: win\n            then: Library/bin/grb_jitpackage.exe\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/DrTimothyAldenDavis/GraphBLAS\n  repository: https://github.com/DrTimothyAldenDavis/GraphBLAS\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: SuiteSparse:GraphBLAS is a full implementation of the GraphBLAS standard\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - grlee77\n    - jakirkham\n    - basnijholt\n    - minrk\n    - jayfurmanek\n    - jim22k\n    - eriknw\n",
